        <section id="operand-and-operator"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>Operand and operator</h2>
              <h3>Operand</h3>
<p>An Operand is the term used to describe an object within the code that is capable of being changed or manipulated in some way.</p>
<h3>Operator</h3>
<p>An Operator is the term used to define those objects within the code that affect that change or manipulation to the Operands. This is either done as a prefix (before the operand) an infix (between operands) or a postfix (after the operands).</p>
<p>So, when looked at together the Operands are the elements which the operators operate upon. In its simplest form, think, 1 + 1, in this case the ones are both Operands and the plus symbol the Operator as that is the thing that affects the two numbers to complete the sum.</p>
<p>Take a look at a snippet of code below from our <em>Javascript example</em>, can you identify which elements are operators and which are operands?</p>

              
              <div class="c-code"><pre class="language-js"><code class="language-js"><span class="highlight-line">sum_of_inputs <span class="token operator">=</span> input_1 <span class="token operator">+</span> input_2</span></code></pre>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
